00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:19.390
Meredith hits on you a lot.

246
00:12:20.270 --> 00:12:23.570
And there's a few moments I'm like, I don't know how he got through that.

247
00:12:23.570 --> 00:12:28.930
But there's some in the, in the, you know, they're at the table in the snack room.

248
00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:29.850
In the break room.

249
00:12:30.150 --> 00:12:30.250
Yeah.

250
00:12:30.490 --> 00:12:30.970
Yeah.

251
00:12:31.190 --> 00:12:35.590
And she's right up on me a couple of times, like full body on me, you know?

252
00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:36.670
And it's so funny.

253
00:12:36.910 --> 00:12:38.010
It's so funny.

254
00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:45.350
We have to talk to you about a few sort of big epic office episodes that are legendary with the caSt.

255
00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:46.930
And one of them is Work Bus.

256
00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:48.410
Work Bus.

257
00:12:48.670 --> 00:12:49.150
Yes.

258
00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:51.290
What do you remember about Work Bus?

259
00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:52.750
Oh, boy.

260
00:12:53.890 --> 00:13:00.610
Well, the, like, behind the scenes, a little BTST, or just like the episode.

261
00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:03.670
Well, you know, we all called it Death Bus.

262
00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:04.730
Yeah.

263
00:13:05.570 --> 00:13:08.490
I remember Bryan Cranston directed that episode.

264
00:13:08.670 --> 00:13:11.870
And I remember the fumes.

265
00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:15.890
I remember the, I remember there was almost no air conditioning.

266
00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:20.950
But even when it was on, it would be on for like 20 seconds as we did a turnaround.

267
00:13:20.970 --> 00:13:24.430
You're like, that's not long enough to cool off a bus full of 20 people.

268
00:13:24.430 --> 00:13:34.770
I remember the fumes from, you know, because it's on a trailer or whatnot, the fumes billowing in and that being a real issue.

269
00:13:35.810 --> 00:13:49.070
I remember being on the road and timing out when things happened because you had to get the same, you know, background on each side as you kind of cross-covered people.

270
00:13:49.070 --> 00:13:51.910
So that was a high bar, too clear.

271
00:13:52.270 --> 00:13:58.350
Jake, I'm pretty sure, too, when we did that big swerve, that's when you slid into me.

272
00:13:58.750 --> 00:13:59.610
That sounds right.

273
00:13:59.850 --> 00:14:03.490
And then I slammed into the wall, that window.

274
00:14:03.970 --> 00:14:04.210
Yeah.

275
00:14:04.270 --> 00:14:05.390
Are we sure that was me?

276
00:14:05.510 --> 00:14:07.490
I mean, that could have been any man.

277
00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:09.050
Yeah, that sounds right.

278
00:14:09.050 --> 00:14:10.130
Anyone on the bus.

279
00:14:10.130 --> 00:14:11.870
Someone, was it you?

280
00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:15.730
Somebody hit their head on that turn.

281
00:14:15.990 --> 00:14:17.410
Someone's head hit the window.

282
00:14:17.590 --> 00:14:18.250
There was a moment of.

283
00:14:18.730 --> 00:14:19.530
It was me.

284
00:14:19.530 --> 00:14:20.270
I just also.

285
00:14:20.430 --> 00:14:21.230
I hit my head.

286
00:14:23.810 --> 00:14:27.350
Look, years later, my deepest apologies.

287
00:14:28.390 --> 00:14:29.610
This is gotcha journalism.

288
00:14:29.850 --> 00:14:35.950
Have I been brought on to be shamed for propulsion of body sliding across seat?

289
00:14:37.110 --> 00:14:38.530
You have not, Jake.

290
00:14:38.530 --> 00:14:44.150
And we want you to know that Bryan Cranston has gone on the record discussing these calamities.

291
00:14:44.470 --> 00:14:45.570
They are well-known.

292
00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:50.010
Ellie has gone on the record about peeing her pants in the bus.

293
00:14:51.650 --> 00:14:52.890
It was a day.

294
00:14:53.210 --> 00:14:54.310
I do remember.

295
00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:55.690
Maybe it was John.

296
00:14:56.430 --> 00:14:57.230
Maybe it was Rain.

297
00:14:57.230 --> 00:15:06.450
And we stopped at one point and they, one or both of them got off and were like, I'm not getting back on this bus until you sort this out.

298
00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:10.970
But there was a real moment of like, hey, it's not just actors complaining in here.

299
00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:13.470
There's, you should, this should be addressed.

300
00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:19.130
And then the other was, there was silence on that bus for a little while.

301
00:15:19.130 --> 00:15:28.210
And Ed, from the back, was like, 17 cast members of the office died today.

302
00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:32.010
Like, just peppered it out there and everybody started laughing.

303
00:15:32.010 --> 00:15:32.710
Did his Tom Brokaw.

304
00:15:32.970 --> 00:15:38.590
That he did his Brokaw, announcing that like the entire cast had been killed in a traffic accident.

305
00:15:38.590 --> 00:15:40.250
And I was like, that's hilarious.

306
00:15:40.550 --> 00:15:41.950
Like, that is so funny.

307
00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:46.850
In this moment where everyone's like, I can't, I can't, I will not stand for that.

308
00:15:46.950 --> 00:15:52.030
You know, silently stewing that he was like, from the deep, deep back of the bus.

309
00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:53.430
That's awesome.

310
00:15:54.490 --> 00:15:56.610
Well, we remember Work Bus the same.

311
00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:59.130
That's really similar to our memories.

312
00:15:59.570 --> 00:16:00.970
This is a crazy question.

313
00:16:01.150 --> 00:16:02.350
I feel like I know the answer.

314
00:16:02.630 --> 00:16:07.490
Did you really grow a mustache for Movember, for the episode Movember?

315
00:16:07.490 --> 00:16:09.370
Or was that a fakey mustache?

316
00:16:09.870 --> 00:16:12.490
I have such a weak, such a weak mustache.

317
00:16:13.010 --> 00:16:18.770
I'll grow like an Amish kind of, you know, chin strap overnight.

318
00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:23.490
But the one thing I pine for is like a proper, I would just live with a cool,

319
00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:25.270
Selic mustache if I could.

320
00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:27.490
So no, I didn't, I didn't do it.

321
00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:33.530
They cut my hair, you know, just to maintain that men's bob that I had.

322
00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:41.410
And then used the ends of those clippings to make my own little rat stash that they taped on.

323
00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:45.730
They used your own hair clippings to make that mustache?

324
00:16:46.350 --> 00:16:47.070
Yeah, yeah.

325
00:16:47.390 --> 00:16:51.250
I mean, it's kind of, it's both like overkill and also real attention to detail.

326
00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:51.910
It's pretty cool.

327
00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:57.950
Also better than being like, I don't know, this is someone's hair and we'll just put it on.

328
00:16:58.270 --> 00:16:59.310
Oh, God.

329
00:16:59.630 --> 00:17:06.890
I think you got the better deal than what Paul Lieberstein got because that was like a small woodland creature on his upper lip.

330
00:17:10.190 --> 00:17:11.530
That's got to be fake too, right?

331
00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:12.330
That's not, he didn't grow.

332
00:17:12.350 --> 00:17:13.610
Oh, that was for sure fake.

333
00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:14.390
Okay.

334
00:17:15.270 --> 00:17:19.450
I have to ask you about all of those diehard scenes.

335
00:17:19.770 --> 00:17:23.990
I mean, I watched all the deleted scenes and there were so many, Jake.

336
00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:25.230
It was physical too.

337
00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:29.670
Like you were like rolling on the ground and standing up and it was amazing.

338
00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:34.730
Yeah, I had, you know, my girlfriend was in New York.

339
00:17:34.910 --> 00:17:39.630
So I was in LA alone and had no kids or pets or responsibilities.

340
00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:43.010
So that is all just like memorized.

341
00:17:43.110 --> 00:17:52.270
And I think, you know, as an indication of like my obsession sometimes with things, I think it had been lightly suggested.

342
00:17:52.270 --> 00:17:57.650
Like here's some scenes that'd be fun for you to, you know, so we could pull clips from it.

343
00:17:57.750 --> 00:18:04.910
And then I memorized the first like 40 minutes of that movie or something, you know, like the cadence of it, the thing.

344
00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:11.670
And also personally, cause I was like, I don't want anyone who loves diehard to watch this and be like, what is he doing?

345
00:18:12.350 --> 00:18:13.530
That's not what happens.

346
00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:14.190
You know?

347
00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:15.510
You had so much detail.

348
00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:19.530
Like you would say a line and then you'd go ring, ning, ning, ning, ning, ning, ning, ning, ning, ning.

349
00:18:20.170 --> 00:18:22.550
You're not going to come here.

350
00:18:22.710 --> 00:18:23.610
Ring, ning, ning, ning.

351
00:18:23.710 --> 00:18:25.810
I'm like, what is, what is the ring, ning, ning, ning?

352
00:18:25.970 --> 00:18:27.150
Is it the big fan?

353
00:18:27.430 --> 00:18:28.270
What is that?

354
00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:29.070
Yeah.

355
00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:31.470
I guess I built out a whole world.

356
00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:31.790
Yeah.

357
00:18:31.850 --> 00:18:34.530
I thought it would be really fun to go for it or whoever.

358
00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:39.590
I think also, again, like whoever wrote that episode had approached me and been like, you should go for it.

359
00:18:39.790 --> 00:18:40.470
Robert Padnick.

360
00:18:40.630 --> 00:18:41.470
He loves diehard.

361
00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:41.910
Yeah.

362
00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:42.510
He's brilliant.

363
00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:43.210
Oh yeah.

364
00:18:43.210 --> 00:18:43.750
He's amazing.

365
00:18:44.110 --> 00:18:48.910
When, when I watched all those deleted scenes, I was like, this was hours of memorization.

366
00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:51.450
You must've spent so many days on that.

367
00:18:51.930 --> 00:18:57.150
I would just be in my trailer, you know, in that parking lot, just watching diehard.

368
00:18:57.330 --> 00:18:59.650
Like, I don't even know if it was on my phone.

369
00:18:59.810 --> 00:19:04.410
I'm trying to, maybe they gave me a DVD of it and I could like play it on the little thing in the trailer or whatever.

370
00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:06.310
But like, yeah, yeah.

371
00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:08.210
Genuinely hours and hours and hours.

372
00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:12.270
Well, it's fantastic for anyone out there that has the DVDs.

373
00:19:12.410 --> 00:19:18.810
I highly recommend watching all of Jake's performances outside of the episode that live in the deleted scene.

374
00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:23.060
I'm like, it was my one chance.

375
00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:24.060
Delete it.

376
00:19:24.060 --> 00:19:29.480
Jake, I have this memory of you joining the cast for that final season.

377
00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:35.360
And there was a group of us who were so delighted to have new people there.

378
00:19:35.620 --> 00:19:40.580
It was like, you and Clark, I'm afraid we were annoying.

379
00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:41.580
I'm afraid.

380
00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:46.000
Like, cause we had all talked to each other for eight full years.

381
00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:49.440
And now, finally, there were some new people.

382
00:19:49.980 --> 00:19:53.440
And it was the most exciting thing.

383
00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:59.260
I would actually try to, like, not overwhelm you with talking your ear off.

384
00:19:59.440 --> 00:20:03.300
Because we were just, I mean, the crew included.

385
00:20:03.460 --> 00:20:05.840
There was not a new face for so long.

386
00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:09.020
I have to know, like, how was it for you?

387
00:20:09.420 --> 00:20:11.680
Well, I've never thought of it in those terMs.

388
00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:18.000
Like, it's never crossed my mind to go, all right, you had almost 10 years of working with the same people for months and months.

389
00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:25.680
And, like, the bond that that brings, you also go, man, it'd be nice to not know everyone's life story that I'm here with.

390
00:20:25.940 --> 00:20:26.320
Exactly.

391
00:20:26.600 --> 00:20:28.160
It'd be nice to have a little mystery.

392
00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:28.920
Yeah.

393
00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:40.940
Um, I, you know, at the time, I just thought, I was just so consumed with, like, you know, don't mess this up.

394
00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:44.060
Don't be weird around these people.

395
00:20:44.620 --> 00:20:46.360
Don't, you know what I mean?

396
00:20:46.420 --> 00:20:49.460
Like, don't fan out and get weird.

397
00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:54.020
And, you know, like, just show up and do your thing and leave.

398
00:20:54.640 --> 00:20:56.420
Don't try to make it social.

399
00:20:56.420 --> 00:20:59.480
Don't, you know, like, nobody's excited that you're here, Jake.

400
00:20:59.720 --> 00:21:00.800
Just do your thing.

401
00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:06.880
So, it's funny years later to hear you go, like, we were thrilled to have new people here.

402
00:21:07.420 --> 00:21:12.060
Um, and that you were like, I'm going to play it cool because that's what I was doing.

403
00:21:12.240 --> 00:21:13.960
I was fully being like, I'm going to play it cool.

404
00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:14.660
I'm going to play it cool.

405
00:21:14.800 --> 00:21:16.080
Like, I'm, hey, it's nice to meet you.

406
00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:19.100
As if I've never seen the show and didn't know it existed.

407
00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:21.040
Instead of, like, I've seen every episode.

408
00:21:21.320 --> 00:21:22.400
It's my favorite program.

409
00:21:22.540 --> 00:21:22.980
You know what I mean?

410
00:21:23.540 --> 00:21:24.540
Oh, my gosh, yes.

411
00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:27.780
Okay, so I just watched the episode with my teens.

412
00:21:27.780 --> 00:21:30.480
We did a little bit of a office marathon last night.

413
00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:33.060
And we watched the beginning of Moving On.

414
00:21:33.320 --> 00:21:35.160
And Andy comes back.

415
00:21:35.680 --> 00:21:38.900
And he's forgotten that your name is Pete.

416
00:21:39.220 --> 00:21:40.700
He just calls you Plop.

417
00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:43.860
And he's like, Aaron is hooking up with some guy named Pete.

418
00:21:44.060 --> 00:21:48.700
You have a great moment where you're like, I think Andy's called me Plop for so long.

419
00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:50.380
He's forgotten my name is Pete.

420
00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:51.440
Yeah.

421
00:21:51.440 --> 00:21:53.240
That runner was hilarious.

422
00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:55.160
Which is my name, Pete.

423
00:21:55.940 --> 00:22:00.780
Like, I think then I, now you're, like, I say it again to the camera crew, basically.

424
00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:04.620
To be like, that's me, just in case you guys are also not caught up.

425
00:22:04.740 --> 00:22:06.100
I'm, I'm Pete.

426
00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:14.160
Yeah, that was, you know, the, is that, Jon Favreau directed one of those.

427
00:22:14.160 --> 00:22:16.880
It might be that, that episode.

428
00:22:17.120 --> 00:22:17.320
Yes.

429
00:22:17.540 --> 00:22:18.780
And then they made it two.

430
00:22:19.140 --> 00:22:20.640
They made it two parts, right.

431
00:22:21.020 --> 00:22:21.180
Yeah.

432
00:22:21.560 --> 00:22:23.180
I loved working with him.

433
00:22:23.580 --> 00:22:30.900
It was, like, maybe my favorite big name guest director that we had outside of Harold Ramis.

434
00:22:31.220 --> 00:22:31.400
Yeah.

435
00:22:31.560 --> 00:22:32.580
With Jon Favreau.

436
00:22:32.980 --> 00:22:37.340
And I know, I'm sorry, that was before he joined us.

437
00:22:37.800 --> 00:22:39.320
Yeah, he's a hero.

438
00:22:39.320 --> 00:22:40.260
Mm-hmm.

439
00:22:40.580 --> 00:22:40.900
Legend.

440
00:22:41.740 --> 00:22:41.900
Yeah.

441
00:22:42.300 --> 00:22:43.660
But Jon Favreau was amazing.

442
00:22:43.860 --> 00:22:50.420
And they, so, his episode was so good that they didn't want to cut a single minute from it.

443
00:22:50.560 --> 00:22:52.720
And so they made it supersized.

444
00:22:53.100 --> 00:22:53.760
Yes.

445
00:22:54.380 --> 00:22:55.040
Yeah.

446
00:22:55.040 --> 00:22:58.100
What I remember that he, well, I guess I have a couple things.

447
00:22:58.220 --> 00:23:02.300
One is, like, I remember before every scene, he would just go over the moment before.

448
00:23:03.080 --> 00:23:03.520
Yes.

449
00:23:03.520 --> 00:23:08.720
He would just, as a group, go, like, hey, just to be clear, this person's back.

450
00:23:08.980 --> 00:23:10.540
You're feeling this way about it.

451
00:23:10.660 --> 00:23:12.880
Maybe you guys feel something else about it.

452
00:23:12.920 --> 00:23:13.240
I don't know.

453
00:23:13.320 --> 00:23:14.060
That's up to you.

454
00:23:14.760 --> 00:23:16.700
And you're worried about this.

455
00:23:17.620 --> 00:23:20.100
And earlier, we found out about that.

456
00:23:20.220 --> 00:23:21.500
So let's just keep that in mind.

457
00:23:22.180 --> 00:23:23.320
And, uh, go ahead.

458
00:23:23.320 --> 00:23:28.900
And, you know, like, that clarity, just going back to the basics of, like, where are you coming from?

459
00:23:28.920 --> 00:23:29.560
Where are you going?

460
00:23:29.720 --> 00:23:30.400
What are you trying to get?

461
00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:32.480
Yeah, just good scene work.

462
00:23:32.480 --> 00:23:33.840
He was so good with that.

463
00:23:34.500 --> 00:23:34.840
Yeah.

464
00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:41.900
And letting that add up to something, you know, that if you had all the pieces, then in the edit, he could go, oh, I'll build it from here, you know.

465
00:23:41.900 --> 00:23:53.280
And also that he knew story-wise, there was something where I come in, talking to Aaron, I'm asking about mail, Andy's back.

466
00:23:53.820 --> 00:23:59.280
And there was some kind of back and forth, like, two or four or five lines, something like that.

467
00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:02.840
And John was like, just, I know what they're trying to do here.

468
00:24:03.820 --> 00:24:06.000
I don't think this really accomplishes it.

469
00:24:06.220 --> 00:24:13.440
Just come in and look through the mail and look down to Ellie.

470
00:24:14.360 --> 00:24:21.300
And she'll sort of look up to you, and you can smile, and then just take your mail and go to the desk.

471
00:24:21.720 --> 00:24:23.020
And I was like, amazing.

472
00:24:23.480 --> 00:24:27.740
Like, that he understood to go, like, maybe we don't need this dialogue.

473
00:24:28.140 --> 00:24:29.060
Like, just, we get it.

474
00:24:29.400 --> 00:24:32.000
We see two people who are into each other.

475
00:24:32.140 --> 00:24:34.440
We see this little quiet, private connection.

476
00:24:34.440 --> 00:24:41.740
And, like, that means more to the story and to the audience than being quippy with each other.

477
00:24:41.900 --> 00:24:45.920
Like, that's not actually the thing that those two characters have found in each other.

478
00:24:46.060 --> 00:24:47.620
It's not a sparring partner.

479
00:24:47.780 --> 00:24:49.260
It's someone that they like to be with.

480
00:24:49.560 --> 00:24:50.520
So just be with them.

481
00:24:50.900 --> 00:24:53.840
You know, like, he could see that stuff and go, oh, man.

482
00:24:54.560 --> 00:24:57.680
And I feel like I'm talking a lot, but I just love the show.

483
00:24:57.820 --> 00:25:02.140
And I don't know, this is, like, a door to memory lane that I didn't know existed.

484
00:25:02.140 --> 00:25:03.160
